					<div class="pdf24_01" style="left:35.1333em;top:29.9338em;"><span class="pdf24_23 pdf24_11 pdf24_09" style="word-spacing:0em;">Social security number &nbsp;</span></div>
					<div class="pdf24_01" style="left:3em;top:30.2273em;"><span class="pdf24_20 pdf24_15 pdf24_09" style="word-spacing:0em;">Enter your TIN in the appropriate box. The TIN provided must match the name given on line 1 to avoid &nbsp;</span></div>
					<div class="pdf24_01" style="left:3em;top:31.0273em;"><span class="pdf24_20 pdf24_15 pdf24_09" style="word-spacing:0em;">backup withholding. For individuals, this is generally your social security number (SSN). However, for a &nbsp;</span></div>
					<div class="pdf24_01" style="left:3em;top:31.8273em;"><span class="pdf24_20 pdf24_15 pdf24_09" style="word-spacing:0em;">resident alien, sole proprietor, or disregarded entity, see the instructions for Part I, later. For other &nbsp;</span></div>
					<div class="pdf24_01" style="left:3em;top:32.624em;"><span class="pdf24_20 pdf24_15 pdf24_09" style="word-spacing:-0.0001em;">entities, it is your employer identification number (EIN). If you do not have a number, see </span><span class="pdf24_21 pdf24_22 pdf24_09" style="word-spacing:0em;">How to get a &nbsp;</span></div>
